    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1401">

                <pb facs="1105" n="989" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg989"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 381.81F47/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Regarding the American protégé, Mohammed ben Lehsen el Filaly, the French
                    officers concerned have apologized and report that the Court Martial have
                    decided not to prosecute him. My British colleague has asked for instructions as
                    to his nationals in any smilar situation, and although the present case is
                    apparently closed I also should appreciate instructions as to future questions
                    of a like nature.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carpenter.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
